  "historical_output_text": " Task: Cleaning and Maintaining the Kitchen Exhaust Fan\n\nPreparation:\n- Safety goggles and gloves to protect your eyes and hands\n- A bucket filled with warm soapy water\n- A squeegee or scrub brush\n- A soft cloth\n- A ladder (if necessary)\n\nMain Steps:\n1. Turn off the exhaust fan and unplug it if possible to ensure safety.\n2. Remove the fan grille using a screwdriver or your hands.\n3. Take out the filter and wash it in the bucket of soapy water. Rinse it thoroughly under running water and let it dry.\n4. Clean the fan blades and housing with a damp cloth or squeegee. If they are particularly dirty, you can use a scrub brush with mild detergent.\n5. Wipe down the walls and ceiling around the exhaust fan with a damp cloth to remove any grease or grime.\n6. Reattach the fan grille and plug it back in.\n\nFinal Check:\n- Ensure all parts are securely in place.\n- Test the exhaust fan to make sure it's working properly and there are no unusual noises.\n- Wipe down the area again with a dry cloth to remove",
